{"parentUuid":"2c76f849-1885-4ddc-9828-7fcec44901a1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgxcYsUL77c8VFbKmgR3G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qq39XRcvNBzRS3mwutAEJy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 467,482p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; echo ----; sed -n 562,572p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; echo ----; sed -n 981,1000p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md","description":"Read Spec 1 §40, §47, §80"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3993,"cache_read_input_tokens":347040,"output_tokens":218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3993,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":218,"cache_read_input_tokens":347040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3993,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3993},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":1568,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Qq39XRcvNBzRS3mwutAEJy":{"command":"cd /Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern && sed -n 467,482p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; echo ----; sed -n 562,572p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md; echo ----; sed -n 981,1000p specs/ERN_Memory_Model_Specification_v0.1.md","description":"Read Spec 1 §40, §47, §80"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01Qq39XRcvNBzRS3mwutAEJy":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b5aae7a8-a551-4389-a660-7ba6b5b44023","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgxcYrjwRoZG8e7pgsgp7","requestRef":"8ff96e12-cef7-4ca9-a940-3d3b2a96b32b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"72404be3-60da-4697-8a08-f40565bad49c","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:08:47.136Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
{"parentUuid":"72404be3-60da-4697-8a08-f40565bad49c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0a3077be-f3d6-44b7-a169-c1486d08c4f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qq39XRcvNBzRS3mwutAEJy","type":"tool_result","content":"## 40. Logical Places, Leaves, and Ownership\n\nA place has an identity, optionally a structural parent, an abstract `kind`, an owner `owner : Frame | Place`, and a logical death marker. Structural parenthood `partOf(p,q)` describes the subplaces of a value; `owner` describes **who keeps the storage** of a root place valid. An owned place may lie outside its owner's direct footprint; ownership and composition are therefore distinct.\n\nA **leaf** is a place with no structural children. `footprint(p)` contains the leaves of `p`, and access rights over a place are evaluated on those leaves. Places transitively owned by a value are not automatically leaves of its `footprint`. A logical unit of the access discipline does not automatically constitute an additional allocation in the elementary memory machine.\n\nA place `p` is **usable** (`Usable(s,p)`) if and only if:\n\n1. `p` exists and is not marked dead;\n2. if its owner is a frame, that frame belongs to the stack;\n3. if its owner is a place `q`, then `q` is itself usable and the chain terminates at a frame in the stack.\n\nAn ownership cycle makes no place usable. `placeFrame(p)` is the terminal frame of this chain when `p` is usable. Structural parts share their parent's owner and death marker. A value may be logically ended by `endUse` without the place that contained it becoming unusable; the substorages it owned may, however, die.\n\nA **root place** has no structural parent. Every **usable** root place has a root authority of own mode `Modify`, with no origin, held exactly by that place's owner (`RootHeld`). This authority cannot be transferred in isolation; root ownership follows a legal transfer of the owning value when necessary.\n\n----\n## 47. Initial State\n\nThe kernel's initial state contains only base frame 0 and the declared static storage. Every static leaf has its declared initial state, `Init` or `Uninit`. The roots of static places directly owned by frame 0 have a root `Modify` authority held by that frame; a static may also be owned by another static, in which case its root authority is held by the latter. The ownership graph of statics is acyclic: no static is owned, directly or transitively, by itself. The initial state invents no dynamic allocation, derived authority, or implicit anchor. The initial arena registry belongs to library state and is empty. The initial frame does not exit.\n\n## 48. External Parametric Contract\n\n`K` contains the predicates `DeclaredDisjoint`, `SharedMutable`, `Pinned`, `ExternalDone`, `Deallocable`, `FreeCompat`, and `Satisfiable`. Their obligations are specified in Section 80. `K` can neither fabricate access rights nor remove an obligation of the Charter. The predicate `Invalidates` is not part of this contract.\n\n# VII. Invariants of Reachable States\n\nMachine states are subject to structural, validity, and exclusivity requirements preserved by permitted transitions under their declared external contracts.\n----\n## 80. Parametric Contracts of the Access Discipline\n\nA contract `K` parameterizes rules of the access discipline without fabricating permissions. A safe abstraction using part of `K` must prove or fulfill the corresponding obligation; an unestablished precondition is not a language guarantee.\n\n| Contract | External obligation |\n|---|---|\n| `DeclaredDisjoint` | `DDSound(K)`: no falsely declared disjoint region when leaves can overlap |\n| `Pinned` | I5, prohibition of incompatible physical moves; `StaticPinnedBottom` for pinned statics |\n| `SharedMutable` | Applicable shared-mutation discipline, with correct rights and synchronization |\n| `ExternalDone` | External use of storage has ended when `unpin` is permitted |\n| `Deallocable` | The place belongs to a unit that can actually be freed |\n| `FreeCompat` | Opaque deallocation authority is compatible with the unit being freed |\n| `Satisfiable` | The provider can satisfy the requested shape **in the current state** |\n\nStructural conditions of `free`, dependencies, and the derived library `reset` carry the relevant invalidation obligations. Physical justification of `DDSound` must be established by a realization consistent with memory layouts and Section 82.\n\n## 81. Boundaries Remaining to Be Specified\n\nThis specification **does not by itself determine**: concurrency and synchronization effects (Spec 2); control-flow analysis, `defer`, and by-value calling conventions (Spec 3); representation criteria and typed formation of accesses (Spec 4); representation of library metadata, address width, encodings, and alignment/ABI obligations (Spec 11); or final translation of `noalias` properties (Spec 13). Leaving a rule open does not authorize a safe interface to cause UB; the implementation must fulfill or reject the obligations before exposing the operation to safe code.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d74de278-f3e2-4156-ab5a-2811b142a1a2","timestamp":"2026-11-12T07:08:48.122Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 40. Logical Places, Leaves, and Ownership\n\nA place has an identity, optionally a structural parent, an abstract `kind`, an owner `owner : Frame | Place`, and a logical death marker. Structural parenthood `partOf(p,q)` describes the subplaces of a value; `owner` describes **who keeps the storage** of a root place valid. An owned place may lie outside its owner's direct footprint; ownership and composition are therefore distinct.\n\nA **leaf** is a place with no structural children. `footprint(p)` contains the leaves of `p`, and access rights over a place are evaluated on those leaves. Places transitively owned by a value are not automatically leaves of its `footprint`. A logical unit of the access discipline does not automatically constitute an additional allocation in the elementary memory machine.\n\nA place `p` is **usable** (`Usable(s,p)`) if and only if:\n\n1. `p` exists and is not marked dead;\n2. if its owner is a frame, that frame belongs to the stack;\n3. if its owner is a place `q`, then `q` is itself usable and the chain terminates at a frame in the stack.\n\nAn ownership cycle makes no place usable. `placeFrame(p)` is the terminal frame of this chain when `p` is usable. Structural parts share their parent's owner and death marker. A value may be logically ended by `endUse` without the place that contained it becoming unusable; the substorages it owned may, however, die.\n\nA **root place** has no structural parent. Every **usable** root place has a root authority of own mode `Modify`, with no origin, held exactly by that place's owner (`RootHeld`). This authority cannot be transferred in isolation; root ownership follows a legal transfer of the owning value when necessary.\n\n----\n## 47. Initial State\n\nThe kernel's initial state contains only base frame 0 and the declared static storage. Every static leaf has its declared initial state, `Init` or `Uninit`. The roots of static places directly owned by frame 0 have a root `Modify` authority held by that frame; a static may also be owned by another static, in which case its root authority is held by the latter. The ownership graph of statics is acyclic: no static is owned, directly or transitively, by itself. The initial state invents no dynamic allocation, derived authority, or implicit anchor. The initial arena registry belongs to library state and is empty. The initial frame does not exit.\n\n## 48. External Parametric Contract\n\n`K` contains the predicates `DeclaredDisjoint`, `SharedMutable`, `Pinned`, `ExternalDone`, `Deallocable`, `FreeCompat`, and `Satisfiable`. Their obligations are specified in Section 80. `K` can neither fabricate access rights nor remove an obligation of the Charter. The predicate `Invalidates` is not part of this contract.\n\n# VII. Invariants of Reachable States\n\nMachine states are subject to structural, validity, and exclusivity requirements preserved by permitted transitions under their declared external contracts.\n----\n## 80. Parametric Contracts of the Access Discipline\n\nA contract `K` parameterizes rules of the access discipline without fabricating permissions. A safe abstraction using part of `K` must prove or fulfill the corresponding obligation; an unestablished precondition is not a language guarantee.\n\n| Contract | External obligation |\n|---|---|\n| `DeclaredDisjoint` | `DDSound(K)`: no falsely declared disjoint region when leaves can overlap |\n| `Pinned` | I5, prohibition of incompatible physical moves; `StaticPinnedBottom` for pinned statics |\n| `SharedMutable` | Applicable shared-mutation discipline, with correct rights and synchronization |\n| `ExternalDone` | External use of storage has ended when `unpin` is permitted |\n| `Deallocable` | The place belongs to a unit that can actually be freed |\n| `FreeCompat` | Opaque deallocation authority is compatible with the unit being freed |\n| `Satisfiable` | The provider can satisfy the requested shape **in the current state** |\n\nStructural conditions of `free`, dependencies, and the derived library `reset` carry the relevant invalidation obligations. Physical justification of `DDSound` must be established by a realization consistent with memory layouts and Section 82.\n\n## 81. Boundaries Remaining to Be Specified\n\nThis specification **does not by itself determine**: concurrency and synchronization effects (Spec 2); control-flow analysis, `defer`, and by-value calling conventions (Spec 3); representation criteria and typed formation of accesses (Spec 4); representation of library metadata, address width, encodings, and alignment/ABI obligations (Spec 11); or final translation of `noalias` properties (Spec 13). Leaving a rule open does not authorize a safe interface to cause UB; the implementation must fulfill or reject the obligations before exposing the operation to safe code.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b5aae7a8-a551-4389-a660-7ba6b5b44023","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","root":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","branch":"formal/spec2-m4","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"ernlang/ern","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"72404be3-60da-4697-8a08-f40565bad49c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/guygouri/Devlab/ernlang/ern","sessionId":"e6419d94-65c2-4a67-8a07-67ae7e574ad6","version":"2.1.321","gitBranch":"formal/spec2-m4","slug":"replicated-napping-garden"}
